::JOUR_U05_L08_UA_Q01::[MLA.JOUR.DIG.01] Source: Unit 5 Digital Publication Scenario. Project: The journalism staff is preparing a final online package called New Student Guide. Required parts: a digital presentation explaining three key findings, a sequential image strip showing how to find student services, an accurate feature photo, a revised article, and an online publication page. Team Needs: the package must be cohesive, visually accurate, captioned, reviewed, exported, submitted on time, and appropriate for new students and families. Production Risk: one image is outdated, one caption is vague, the article needs final revision, and the team has two days before publication. Question: Unit Assessment Question 1: Which answer best applies Unit 5 digital journalism skills to the New Student Guide package? {
~A. Publish immediately because a deadline is close#Not correct. Step 1: reread the embedded source instead of relying on a general preference. Step 2: locate the audience need, accuracy issue, digital tool, workflow, or publication requirement. Step 3: reject choices that weaken verification, visual accuracy, collaboration, sequence, deadline control, or publication readiness.
=B. Use accurate visuals, logical sequence, revised text, teamwork, and deadline workflow before publication#Correct. Step 1: connect the decision to the MLA journalism standard shown in the item. Step 2: use the embedded source to verify the audience need, accuracy issue, digital tool, workflow, or publication requirement. Step 3: choose the option that protects credible, clear, publication-ready journalism.
~C. Let each media part use a separate purpose and tone#Not correct. Step 1: reread the embedded source instead of relying on a general preference. Step 2: locate the audience need, accuracy issue, digital tool, workflow, or publication requirement. Step 3: reject choices that weaken verification, visual accuracy, collaboration, sequence, deadline control, or publication readiness.
~D. Ignore captions because the article explains everything#Not correct. Step 1: reread the embedded source instead of relying on a general preference. Step 2: locate the audience need, accuracy issue, digital tool, workflow, or publication requirement. Step 3: reject choices that weaken verification, visual accuracy, collaboration, sequence, deadline control, or publication readiness.
}
